  "rationale": "The throughput constraint (>=1 MSPS) is easily satisfied by both iterative and unrolled_k for N<=30 and k>=2, so it is not binding. Accuracy requires data_width >= 11 with rounding (half-LSB = 2^-10) and n_iter >= ~11 to keep CORDIC approximation error below the quantization floor. Area is the sole objective, so the optimal design will use the smallest feasible data_width, n_iter, and guard bits. iterative reuses one micro-rotation stage and is therefore the smallest-area family; unrolled_k replicates k stages and is likely dominated. We allocate 80% of the first-round budget to iterative to pin down the minimum-area feasible point, and 20% to unrolled_k to confirm dominance or find any niche. Ranges are narrowed to the plausible low-area region (W=11..16, N=10..16, small guards) to spend evaluations where the trade-off is steep. We use 60 of the 100 total evaluations this round, reserving 40 for later refinement and full-range Pareto mapping.",
